            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding our shared patient, a 40-year-old male admitted to our department following findings suspicious for acute haematological malignancy. Upon admission, comprehensive diagnostic workup including bone marrow biopsy and immunophenotyping confirmed the diagnosis of Acute Myeloid Leukaemia (AML). Cytogenetic and molecular analyses were performed to further characterise the disease subtype and guide treatment planning. Following multidisciplinary team discussion, the patient was commenced on standard induction chemotherapy according to current AML protocol. The patient tolerated the initial treatment phase with manageable side effects, receiving appropriate supportive care throughout the hospital stay. He is now discharged in stable condition with outpatient haematology follow-up arranged. Please do not hesitate to contact our haematology department should any concerns arise in the interim.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
